          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            This page is used as a hub to gather references about
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category-theoretic
            work (and more widely, other mathematical foundational work) with explicit applications to biology.
          %p
            %em Biology
            can be seen as an umbrella term for a spectrum of scientific domains all interested in studying life, at various
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biological_organisation"} scales
            %a{:href => "https://www.cdc.gov/genomics/about/basics.htm"} DNA mechanisms
            to
            %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Complex_system"} complex systems
            through
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Protein%E2%80%93protein_interaction"} protein interactions
          %h2#categories Categories
          %p This section presents category theoretic models using categories as ways to describe biological mechanisms and relations.
          %h3#ologs Ologs
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ontology"} Ontologies
            are used in
            %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genomics"} genomics
            to classify categories of observable phenomena such as
            %a{:href => "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/doid"} diseases
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gene_Ontology"} gene expressions
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ontology+log"} ontology logs
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            where each arrow describes an aspect of some types of things under study. For example, the following olog describes
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genetic_disorder"} single-gene genetic disorders
