          %p
            The previous construction can then be repeated recursively on the set of labels
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
            %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Organ"} biological organs
            in an individual. Then, the next level
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_2
            (obtained from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
            by following the previous procedure) can be the set of all
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Organ_system"} organ systems
            %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_body"} bodies
            on a fourth level
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_3
          %p
            Note that hyperstructures also require compatibility properties between the labels. In particular, for each level
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S,\omega)
            should be organized into a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∫
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int \Omega
            such that the mappings
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S,\omega) \mapsto \beta
            define a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int \Omega \to \mathbf{Set}
          %h3#bigraphs_calculus_and_calculus
            Bigraphs,
            = succeed "-calculus" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            = succeed "-calculus" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
          %p
            %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bigraph"} Bigraphs
            are a type of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypergraph"} hypergraph-based
            structures that can be linked to
            %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Process_calculus"} process algebras
            such as the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lambda-calculus"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
                \-calculus
            %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%CE%A0-calculus"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
              \-calculus
            and its
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/referenceworkentry/10.1007/978-1-4419-9863-7_767"} stochastic variant
          %p
            Interestingly, it was shown that the
            = succeed "-calculus" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category+theory"} 2-category-theoretic
            setting.
          %p
            A number of bigraph-based formalisms have been proposed to model complex systems, some with a category theoretic flavor. For example,
            %a{:href => "https://www.pure.ed.ac.uk/ws/portalfiles/portal/15231648/Stochastic_Bigraphs.pdf"} stochastic bigraphs
            and their compositions have been used to model
            %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Budding"} membrane budding
            in a biological system.
          %h3#references_6 References
          %p Hyperstructures:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nils+Baas"}> NA Baas
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the Philosophy of Higher Structures
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1805.11943.pdf"} arXiv:1805.11943
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nils+Baas"}> NA Baas
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On Higher Structures
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1509.00403.pdf"} arXiv:1509.00403
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nils+Baas"}> NA Baas
                ,
                %em
                  Extended Memory Evolutive Systems in a Hyperstructure Context. Axiomathes 19, 215–221 (2009),
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10516-009-9066-3"} link
          %p Bigraphs:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robin+Milner"}> R Milner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Bigraphs and Their Algebra
              %p
                Volume 209, 24 April 2008, Pages 5-19,
                %a{:href => "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S157106610800217X"} link
            %li
              %p
                J Krivine,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robin+Milner"} R Milner
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stochastic Bigraphs
                %a{:href => "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1571066108004003"} link
          %p
            Relations between
            = succeed "-calculus," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            = succeed "-calculus" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                S Federhen,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Replication is Recursion; or, Lambda: the Biological Imperative
                %a{:href => "https://www.biorxiv.org/content/biorxiv/early/2015/05/01/018804.full.pdf"} bioarxiv
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aviv_Regev"}> A Regev
                , W Silverman, E Shapiro E,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Representation and simulation of biochemical processes using the pi-calculus process algebra
                %a{:href => "http://psb.stanford.edu/psb-online/proceedings/psb01/regev.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                See the blog post by
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"} John Baez
                %a{:href => "https://johncarlosbaez.wordpress.com/2016/01/02/biology-and-the-pi-calculus/"} Biology and the Pi-Calculus
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Stay"}> M Stay
                , LG Meredith,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higher category models of the pi-calculus
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1504.04311"} arXiv:1504.04311
          %h2#other_references Other references
          %p
            A general discussion on using category theory for biology can be found on the
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2007/11/category_theory_and_biology.html"}> category theory and biology
              \.
          %p Phylogenomics:
          %ul
            %li
              L Pachter, B Sturmfels,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The mathematics of phylogenomics
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0409132"} math/0409132
          %p Cell biology:
          %ul
            %li
              V Noel, D Grigoriev, S Vakulenko, O Radulescu,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Tropical geometries and dynamics of biochemical networks. Application to hybrid cell cycle models
              %a{:href => "http://logic.pdmi.ras.ru/~grigorev/pub/tropical_dynamics_modified.pdf"} pdf
          %p Systems biology:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Robert Rosen,
                %em The representation of biological systems from the standpoint of the theory of categories
                , Bulletin of Mathematical Biophysics, Vol 20. 1958,
                %a{:href => "http://www.few.vu.nl/~rplanque/Onderwijs/MathBio/PapersForProject/Rosen.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                IC Baianu, JF Glazebrook and R Brown,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Category Theory And Higher Dimensional Algebra Approach To Complex Systems Biology, Meta-systems And Ontological Theory Of Levels: Emergence Of Life, Society, Human Consciousness And Artificial Intelligence
                %a{:href => "https://planetmath.org/ACATEGORYTHEORYANDHIGHERDIMENSIONALALGEBRAAPPROACHTOCOMPLEXSYSTEMSBIOLOGYMETASYSTEMSANDONTOLOGICALTHEORYOFLEVELS"} text
            %li
              %p
                Jan-Hendrik S. Hofmeyr,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A biochemically-realisable relational model of the self-manufacturing cell
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biosystems.2021.104463"} doi: 10.1016/j.biosystems.2021.104463
            %li
              %p
                Federico Vega,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The cell as a realization of the (M, R) system
          %p Neuroscience:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                According to
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Gromov"} Mikhail Gromov
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-categories"} n-categories
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jRSqGYJQQM8"} Ergologic and Interfaces Between Languages
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andree+Ehresmann"} AC Ehresmann
                and P S Wlimes,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Towards a theoretical framework for wandering logic intelligence memory evolutive systems
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andree+Ehresmann"}> AC Ehresmann
                , J-P Vanbremeersch,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em The memory evolutive systems as a model of Rosen’s organisms
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andree+Ehresmann"}> AC Ehresmann
                , J-P Vanbremeersch.
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Memory Evolutive Systems: Hierarchy, Emergence, Cognition
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andree+Ehresmann"}> AC Ehresmann
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nils+Baas"} N Baas
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Hyperstructures and memory evolutive systems
              %p Intern. J. Gen. Sys., 33(5):553–568, 2004.
            %li
              %p
                D Pastor, E Beurier,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andree+Ehresmann"} AC Ehresmann
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Interfacing biology, category theory and mathematical statistics
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2009.06832.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The following article views biological systems as information-processing agents, supporting recursion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo &gt;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gt
            function hypothesis
          %ul
            %li
              Sara Imari Walker, Paul C. W. Davies,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The algorithmic origins of life
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2012.0869"} doi
